
# NOTE: Words in parenthesis -- such as (traits) and (emo) -- are used for GROUPING only: they don't define a sub-category.

# Every act in the ontology is either a TASK (mini-plan; bubbles down to
# ACTION sequences at isim time, or to event effects at hsim time) or an
# ACTION (lowest-level motor primitive declared in
# interactive/actions/*.act). `act` is the kind-tree parent for both.

relation

    act (noun)

        # /noun = defines 'task' as a noun
        # For all subsequent definitions:
        # * Assume that they are tasks: //task
        # * Assume that their subject field is is always a human: //sub human
        task (noun) (+ task) (+ sub human)

            # ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
            # abstract tasks - no motors involved
            # ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
            startup
            infer

            pubbing

            # dwell / work: episodic activity-lane tasks (hsim_activity_lanes_
            # plan.md L2). {@self dwell <home>} = "spending the day at home";
            # {@self work <org>} = "working at the workplace" (regardless of the
            # job or which org). Minted begin+end per visit by the household /
            # work lanes (record-dwelling / record-work); the decay pass folds
            # repeated days into a cumulative belief whose count is the
            # attendance frequency.
            dwell                                   (tar structure|org|space)
            work                                    (tar structure|org|space)
            # socialize_at: episodic ad-hoc social-outing memory (activity-lanes
            # L3). {@self socialize_at <venue> /aux <organizer>} = "went out with
            # the company <organizer> assembled, at <venue>". One general label
            # for any friends-gathering (pub night, club, hired hall); the
            # organizer is in aux. Minted begin+end per outing by the social-
            # outing lane (host-social-outing); the decay pass folds repeats into
            # a cumulative belief whose count is the outing frequency.
            socialize_at                            (tar structure)    (aux human)
            # pursue: episodic interest-lane memory (activity-lanes L5).
            # {@self pursue <venue> /aux <domain>} = "pursued my interest
            # <domain> at <venue>" - the domain an `interest` sub-kind, the
            # venue the building hosting it. Minted begin+end per outing by the
            # interest lane (pursue-interest); the decay pass folds repeats into
            # a cumulative belief whose count is the pursuit frequency.
            pursue                                  (tar structure)    (aux ?)
            # worship: churchgoing memory. {@self worship <church>} = "worships
            # at <church>". classify_piety reads it (a worshipper is pious) -
            # the specific label replaces the old vague `attend`. The activity-
            # lanes worship lane (L8) will mint it begin+end per service; the
            # current churchgoing seed mints one ongoing belief (binary piety).
            worship                                 (tar structure)    (obs)
            # indulge: episodic vice-lane memory (activity-lanes L8).
            # {@self indulge <pub> /aux alcohol|gambling} = "indulged in
            # <vice> at <pub>". One general label for the pub vices; the vice
            # kind is in aux. Minted begin+end per episode by the vice lane
            # (the drinking event), feeding pub co-presence; the decay pass
            # folds repeats into a cumulative belief. The sobriety / wealth
            # classifiers read the intoxication + gambling_addiction ATTRS (the
            # standing dispositions), NOT this episodic memory.
            indulge                                 (tar structure)    (aux ?)
            # gather: episodic club/civic-lane memory (activity-lanes L8).
            # {@self gather <clubhouse>} = "attended a gathering at <clubhouse>".
            # Minted begin+end per gathering by the club lane (club_gathering ->
            # hold-club-gathering, which walks the club's member-register and the
            # clubhouse building from the org articles) - giving club premises a
            # co-present membership the incident pass can read. The standing
            # membership stays {@self member_of <club-org>} (the roster).
            gather                                  (tar structure)
            # play_game: a game-playing episode (activity-lanes L8). The target
            # is a per-mind game OBJECT (of a game kind), not a venue - {@self
            # play_game <game>} where <game> isa poker / billiards / ...; the
            # co-players ride on the game object as {<game> participant <person>}
            # (States.mon), the venue as the game's own belief or its aux. The
            # target is baked into the label (vs `play_instrument` for music -
            # genuinely different activities). The disposition to gamble is the
            # `gambling_addiction` ATTR (common.arc), NOT this episode.
            #play_game                               (tar game)    (kind_fold)
            play_game                                              (kind_fold)
            
            # attend: a TASK, never an action - attending changes nothing in the
            # env by itself; the task's rungs (attend_think.hs) propose the SHARED
            # physical acts (enter the venue, dwell there, say_to for the vow).
            # {@self attend <occ>} where <occ> is a per-mind occasion Mental
            # Object (Concepts.mon `occasion`), NOT a venue - the venue is the
            # occasion's own {<occ> venue <building>} belief. The window-start
            # appointment review emits {@self goal {@self attend <occ>}} for an
            # occasion whose date lands in the current window.
            attend                                  (tar occasion)
            # THE LABOUR MARKET tasks (job_search_think.hs / recruit_think.hs) -
            # all bodyless (no motor): the running-task belief is the CONTEXT the
            # decomposition rules key on; the physical work routes through the
            # shared actions (enter / read / say_to) + the clerical write family.
            # seek_work: the job hunt (proposed off the {@self employed} goal).
            # apply: one application to one advert (target = the advert doc).
            # take_up_post: acceptance visit + wage-book read (target = the advert).
            # recruiting: the recruit_staff duty-holder's standing recruitment
            # (target = the org; `recruit` is the accomplice-recruitment act);
            # advertise is its board-posting subtask. (Mail reading needs no
            # task - unread letters at home directly propose the read action.)
            seek_work
            apply                                   (tar ?)
            take_up_post                            (tar ?)
            recruiting                              (tar org)
            advertise                               (tar org)
            # Solitary leisure activities at a venue (activity-lanes L8), the
            # amenity-gated successors to the general `dwell`: what one actually
            # DID there, gated by the venue's rooms. Episodic {@self <act>
            # <venue>}. `read_at` (not `read`, the document-reading action
            # above) = a reading session at a study/library; `dine` needs a
            # dining_room; `rest` is the low-amenity default. Pub drinking stays
            # `indulge`.
            # dine's /aux carries the meal occasion (breakfast / luncheon /
            # tea / supper - Objects.mon `meal` leaves). The evidence
            # layer's consume record reads "dined at <venue>, at <supper>";
            # an absent aux is just "dined at <venue>".
            dine                                    (tar structure|space)    (aux meal)
            # eat - the UNIFIED meal act (meals.hs), one lane for breakfast /
            # lunch / supper (incl. eating out). The act-belief
            # {@self eat [k <meal>] <place>} IS the episodic meal memory (begun at
            # commit, ended at completion): target = the meal-kind occasion, aux =
            # the place eaten at. Supersedes the old per-meal `dine` begin-act lanes
            # + their separate punctual dine records.
            eat                                     (tar meal)         (aux structure|space)
            read_at                                 (tar structure|space)
            rest                                    (tar structure|space)
            # go - the TRAVEL act as a first-class ongoing belief ({@self go
            # <place>}, the begin-act unification): "heading to <place>", its
            # interval the travel time, the completion relocating the actor.
            go                                      (tar ?)
            # go_to_threshold - the counterpart TRAVEL act that arrives at a
            # structure's threshold (front-park, OUTSIDE), not inside a space.
            # The enter chain (enter.hs) mints it to reach a venue's face; the
            # completion front-parks the actor where at-threshold reads true.
            go_to_threshold                         (tar ?)
            # depart - the emigrant's LEAVE-TOWN act (depart_act.hs): the standing
            # {@self depart} goal emigration.hs mints; the act quits the job,
            # releases the home and exits the town permanently. Focusless.
            depart
            # provision - the cook's keep-the-larder-stocked errand (buy
            # food at the grocer, carry it home, stow it in the kitchen).
            # The goal the plan_provisioning think event mints and the
            # meals.hs provisioning acts drain.
            provision                               (tar ?)
            # forage - the STARVATION-tail eat act (meals.hs): a famished NPC
            # consumes one food item from the highest-priority source it can reach
            # (carried > pantry > shop buy/steal). Focusless.
            forage                                  (tar ?)
            # stocktake - the shopkeeper's morning inventory round: walk the
            # premises and validate the believed stock against the shelves
            # (take-stock-of-room, stocktake_macros.hs). The act whose whole
            # PURPOSE is confirming / disproving whereabouts beliefs -
            # deliberate attention, the only sanctioned absence-disproof
            # beyond the goal-attended reach-for-it verify.
            stocktake                               (tar ?)
            # Act-belief labels for the begin-act unification: an act IS an ongoing
            # {@self <label> <target>} belief, so its label must be a defined
            # state/action/task (goal-clause labels alone are not enough). stow -
            # putting a carried item away (burgle / provisioning tail); give_alms -
            # the charity act. (scream is already a defined relation-term.)
            stow                                    (tar ?)
            # make_cache - carve a private hiding spot at home (secret letters,
            # stowed loot). The act (make_cache_act.hs) walks the host-quality
            # ladder and claims/creates the best cache; the deliberation that
            # proposes it is make_secret_cache_think.hs. Target is the home.
            # No (obs): a hiding spot is fashioned unseen (concealment is the point).
            make_cache                              (tar ?)
            # bring - carry what you hold of a KIND to a destination and put it
            # away there ({@self bring [k food] <kitchen>}); decomposes to a put
            # once at the destination. The provisioning carry-home leg. The dest is
            # unconstrained: the act just walks to it and puts down at @self's room,
            # so a room (kitchen) or a structure (home) both work.
            bring                                   (tar ?)  (aux ?)
            give_alms                               (tar ?)
            # burial lane (events/npc-act/convey_corpse.hs + bury.hs). Pure
            # perception, no telepathy: a bereaved NPC CARRIES the body to a
            # church; the co-present priest PERCEIVES the corpse in his church
            # and buries it. convey - the bereaved kin's deposit goal {@self
            # convey <corpse>} (route to a church, relocate the body in).
            # conveyed - the bearer's one-shot "already delivered" marker (bars
            # re-carting the same corpse). bury - the priest's burial-rite
            # act-belief {@self bury <corpse>} (verdict + tombstone + destroy).
            # All (tar ?): a corpse's {isa human} belief is end-dated at death,
            # so the target is not kind-constrainable.
            convey                                  (tar ?)
            conveyed                                (tar ?)
            bury                                    (tar ?)
            # Conversational activities (gossip / catch_up / confide / introduce /
            # confess_fancy / table_talk / mealtime asks) carry no acts of their own:
            # each think composes its wire message ((utterable-msg ...) /
            # (utterable-qs ...)) and proposes the ONE say_to act below.
            acquire                                 (tar object)
            buy                                     (tar ?)
            grant                                   (tar object)               (aux human)

            identify                                (tar object)
            get_acquainted_with                       (tar human)
            seek_answers
            marry
            # Great-split (Item 5) goal-action labels - the npc-think mints
            # {@self goal {@self <verb> <focus>}}, the npc-action routes to the located
            # venue and the completion does the world-commit. Distinct from the
            # existing state/kind terms (retire/borrow/apprentice are already defined
            # elsewhere, so these are fresh verbs): quit_work -> the retirement act;
            # take_loan -> a lender (the creditor focus); back -> a backed man;
            # partner -> a firm one buys into; join_club / resign_club -> a club;
            # seek_indenture -> a master; enroll_child -> a school for the child;
            # engage_staff -> the boss's hire.
            quit_work                               (tar ?)
            take_loan                               (tar human)
            back                                    (tar human)
            partner                                 (tar human)
            join_club                               (tar org)
            resign_club                             (tar org)
            seek_indenture                          (tar human)
            enroll_child                            (tar human)
            engage_staff                            (tar human)

            # hold_meet_run  -> the organiser's on-site marker; promotes open_meet_act
            #                  (summon the field).
            # race_run       -> a summoned competitor's marker; promotes race_act
            #                  (self-simulate performance from OWN attrs).
            # judge_meet     -> the organiser's standing GOAL to declare the winner from
            #                  the race_result beliefs the competitors minted into him.
            # judge_declare  -> the dumb ACT the sporting_judge think proposes once a top
            #                  scorer is cast; its target is that winner.
            hold_meet_run                           (sub human)
            race_run                                (sub human)
            judge_meet                              (tar ?)
            judge_declare                           (tar human)

            # find_building -> the venue-discovery search TASK (find_building.hs). A seek rule
            # maintains {@self find_building [k building <kind>] ?region} while it wants a venue of a
            # kind it knows none of: target = the sought kind, aux = the region to cover. It
            # decomposes STRAIGHT into go_to_threshold hops (front-park at the closest unobserved
            # structure so perception teaches it and its kind); its OUTCOME is /fail once the whole
            # region is covered without finding the kind (find_exhausted). Success is the seeker's
            # own (no-role [k building <kind>]) flipping the moment perception reveals a match.
            find_building                           (tar ?)  (aux ?)
            # staff_household -> the head's STANDING duty to keep their domestic
            # establishment staffed (the window-start think mints it; the emergent
            # act fulfils it). No target: the duty itself, not a specific hire.
            staff_household                         (tar ?)
            sack                                    (tar human)
            promote_staff                           (tar human)
            found_club                              (tar ?)
            # orient -> new_job_orientation: @self goes to the parish and reads the
            # public incorporation register, forming a mental org object (+ isa /
            # founder / record beliefs) per org so the belief-pure casting events
            # (hiring / club_joining / apprenticeship / partnership / appointment)
            # can role over orgs @self KNOWS. No focus - the church is resolved in
            # the act via (venue [k building church]).
            orient                                  (tar ?)
            enrol_primary                           (tar ?)
            enrol_secondary                         (tar ?)
            enrol_university                        (tar ?)

            # Domain-specific tasks
            found                                    (tar org)
            process_title_deed                       (aux structure|space)
            introduce_siblings

            tell_about                              (sub @msgAuthor human)   (tar ?)  (aux @msgAudience human)

            # tell_beliefs: kind-quantified content request. Target is a
            # BELIEF PATTERN like {?sub [k <state_kind>] ? ?} - the pattern
            # IS the query. The (every ...) search is implied by the
            # answering rule, not packaged into the belief (tasks are
            # beliefs, and beliefs cannot contain function calls in their
            # slots; nested-event patterns are admitted via @S). The
            # classifier reads the pattern's label-kind to dispatch the
            # right discourse genre (e.g. [k relationship] ->
            # relationship_description). See Docs/dialogue_nlg_plan.md.
            tell_beliefs                            (sub @msgAuthor human)   (tar @S)  (aux @msgAudience human)

            order
            serve_beer                  (motor mind)    (tar human)    (obs)  (belief_timeout 1800)

            # ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
            # physical tasks - motors are DERIVED, not declared. The closure pass
            # (resolve_task_motors_from_rule_closure) unions the motor bits of every
            # action a task's .ms2 rules reach, so these carry no (motor ...).
            # A manual (motor ...) remains ONLY on tasks whose motors no .ms2 rule
            # can derive - no action-proposing rule under {@self <task>} (approach,
            # explore, locate, drop, give_birth), or a closure that routes its real
            # motors through a goal the pass cannot follow (serve_customer, serve_beer).
            # ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
            #tell                /motor mouth            /sub @msgAuthor human   /tar @msg @excl @S     /aux @msgAudience human
            #ask                 /motor mouth            /sub @msgAuthor human   /tar @qs @excl @S      /aux @msgAudience human
            
            say_to              (motor mouth) (sub @msgAuthor human)   (tar @msg @excl @S) (aux @msgAudience human)

            # The clerical WRITE family (recruit_actions.hs) - pen-changes-paper
            # actions, each producing a DIFFERENT document (an act's args ride its
            # belief, so one generic write cannot carry the varying content; the
            # eat / provision precedent). The writings themselves are COMPOSED in
            # .hs (write-doc-record fields / written-msg letters); the ops only
            # encode them.
            # Actions are PURE PHYSICAL EFFECT: paper and people only (an org is a
            # mental-only object and never an act participant); all recruiter
            # bookkeeping is minted by the *_done think rules off the act outcome.
            # post_advert: write the advert paper (target = the org's articles).
            # record_applicant: an applicants-doc row (target = the applicant).
            # send_letters: the offer + rejection letters (target = the applicants book).
            # enrol: the wage-book row (target = the new hire, aux = the wage book).
            # take_down: remove a filled posting from the board.
            post_advert         (motor right_hand)  (tar @excl articles_of_incorporation)  (aux ?)
            record_applicant    (motor right_hand)  (tar @excl human)
            send_letters        (motor right_hand)  (tar @excl job_application)  (aux human)
            enrol               (motor right_hand)  (tar @excl human)  (aux ?)
            take_down           (motor right_hand)  (tar @excl job_description)

            approach                (motor legs)              (tar @excl)
            enter                   (tar @excl)
            go_entity               (tar @excl)
            go_env_cell             (tar @excl)
            keep_near_and_facing    (tar @excl)
            keep_looking_at_part       (tar @excl)   (aux @excl)
            keep_looking_at_whole      (tar @excl)

            explore             (motor legs)              (tar @excl)
            locate              (motor legs)              (tar @excl)
            
            drop                (motor right_hand)             (tar @excl object)
            # /tar ? : give targets a physical object (the motor task) or a
            # money amount (the Phase 8 charity act-record - a number symbol).
            give                (tar @excl ?)
            receive             (tar @excl object)

            get                 (tar @excl object)
            take                (tar @excl object)
            put                 (tar @excl object)

            read                (motor eyes)  (tar @excl document)   (obs)  (belief_timeout 600)
            write               (tar @excl document)   (obs)  (belief_timeout 600)

            stack_get            (tar object)  (aux stack)
            stack_put            (tar object)  (aux stack)
            stack_browse         (tar stack)
            stack_read           (tar stack)

            # mourn - the action-plan task that drives the visible
            # grieving behaviour (head-burial, hands-to-face, hanging
            # head, crying). The cognitive / affective side of
            # mourning lives in the affect cascade as the `grief`
            # emotion, not here.
            mourn

            give_birth           (motor eyes right_hand legs)
            perceive_attr        (tar ?)

            drink               (tar object)  (obs)

            use_umbrella
            serve_customer      (motor right_hand left_hand legs)   (obs)  (belief_timeout 1800)

            # ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
            # Tasks below are mini-plans that bubble down to an ACTION
            # sequence at isim time and to their hsim event's effect
            # verb at hsim time. construed_act tags drive appraisal
            # categorisation.
            # ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

            # Abstract / cognitive sub-block - no motors. These tasks
            # consume cycle time but emit no env-mutating ACTION sequence.
            withdraw                                            (tar human)
            plead                                               (tar human)
            atone                                               (tar human)              (construed_act honour_act)
            surrender                                           (tar human)
            replace                                             (tar human)

            # urge - influence a target into a sub-task or state. The
            # inner clause is what's being urged, e.g.
            # {mother urge {son avoid {son marry girl}}} composes with
            # the `avoid` state (States.mon). NOT subsumed by `tell`:
            # urging may include non-verbal pressure (withheld
            # affection, threats, ultimatum-via-conduct); the
            # implementing task picks the appropriate ACTION mix.
            urge                                                (tar @S)

            # Social / communication sub-block - tasks that bubble down to
            # SAY / WRITE_DOC ACTION chains. Tags carried over from
            # the deleted (behaviour) block.
            # insult / confront_privately moved into the `speech_act`
            # group at the end of this block.
            humiliate           (motor mouth)                   (tar human)              (construed_act degrade_act wrong_act)
            discredit           (motor mouth)                   (tar human)              (construed_act expose_act betray_act wrong_act)
            expose              (motor mouth)                   (tar @S)                 (construed_act expose_act betray_act wrong_act)
            expose_first        (motor mouth)                   (tar human)              (construed_act expose_act)
            confess_in_person   (motor legs mouth)              (tar human)              (construed_act honour_act)
            confess_letter      (motor eyes right_hand legs)    (tar human)              (construed_act honour_act)
            # divorce: a husband formally puts away an adulterous wife
            # (husband-initiated ONLY - a betrayed wife of the period has
            # no such recourse and releases through confront / expose /
            # humiliate / withdraw instead). Point act-record; the
            # repudiation_act reactions put the disgrace on the PATIENT.
            divorce             (motor mouth)                   (tar human)              (construed_act repudiation_act)
            # report_crime: the lawful-channel deliberation goal. Target is
            # the known wrongdoer, or the wronged PROP when the culprit is
            # unknown (a theft discovered by absence).
            report_crime        (motor mouth eyes right_hand)   (tar ?)
            recruit             (motor mouth)                   (tar human)  (aux ?)

            # Physical / multi-motor sub-block - tasks that compose motor
            # ACTIONs. Motors marked are the typical mix; the
            # implementing isim task may add or substitute depending on
            # method.
            flee                (motor legs)                    (tar human)
            # cry_out - the under-attack victim's scream for help (fight.hs): a
            # focusless 1-minute act that keeps the victim active (not sleeping)
            # while it can neither fight nor flee. (`scream` names a Sounds kind,
            # so the act-label is cry_out.)
            cry_out             (motor mouth)                   (tar ?)
            seduce              (motor mouth legs body)         (tar human)              (construed_act intimacy_act)  (facets blackmailable)
            assault             (motor right_hand left_hand legs)  (tar human)           (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (obs)  (abduct)
            # fight - the EMERGENT-COMBAT goal (the unified think/act model): a melee
            # killer's standing {actor goal {actor fight victim}}, minted by the
            # perpetration melee branch in place of committing the kill. The fight
            # cascade (fight.hs) reaches the victim and strikes 1-minute blows until
            # someone dies (the victim can resist / flee - follow-up).
            fight               (motor right_hand left_hand legs)  (tar human)           (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (obs)
            # kill - ABSTRACT goal task. No method aux: the method is a
            # separate, more-specific leaf task (strangle / shoot / poison
            # / push_from_height / etc.) declared further down. A goal
            # belief like {actor goal {actor kill victim}} expresses
            # "actor wants victim killed by any means". At perpetration
            # time the substrate-driven row picks a concrete leaf
            # method-task; the anchor minted is that leaf-task belief
            # (e.g. {actor strangle victim}), NOT {actor kill victim
            # /aux <method>}. Goals can also target the END STATE
            # directly: {actor goal {victim condition dead}} - then the
            # actor doesn't even need to do the killing themselves.
            kill                                                (tar human)                (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (facets reportable_crime blackmailable)
            kidnap              (motor legs right_hand left_hand)  (tar human)             (construed_act coercion_act threaten_act wrong_act)  (theme coercive_to)  (facets reportable_crime)  (obs)
            steal               (motor legs right_hand)         (tar human)                (construed_act appropriation_act wrong_act)  (theme thief_to)  (facets reportable_crime blackmailable)
            # Goal-level umbrella tasks that the deliberate event mints
            # as goal-clause inner labels. Their leaf method-tasks
            # (declared below) are what actually get performed and
            # recorded as anchors at perpetration time.
            coerce                                              (tar human)  (aux ?)       (construed_act coercion_act wrong_act)  (facets reportable_crime)
            punish                                              (tar human)                (construed_act harm_act)
            hurt                                                (tar human)                (construed_act harm_act)
            # tamper - PREPARATION for a perpetration; the trap-fire event
            # mints the appraisable kill / harm record when the trap
            # fires. No construed_act tag at the task level.
            tamper              (motor right_hand)              (tar object)  (aux ?)
            # add_substance - perpetrator subject; substance target;
            # vessel in aux. Preparation - no tag.
            add_substance       (motor right_hand)              (tar object)  (aux object)
            frame                                               (tar human)  (aux ?)     (construed_act harm_act betray_act wrong_act)  (facets reportable_crime)
            # bribe - functional inverse of coerce. Means-of-pressure;
            # the appraisable harm is whatever gets done with the bought
            # compliance, so no construed_act tag here.
            bribe               (motor right_hand mouth)        (tar human)  (aux ?)     (facets reportable_crime)
            defraud                                             (tar human)              (construed_act appropriation_act wrong_act betray_act)  (theme thief_to)  (facets reportable_crime blackmailable)
            embezzle                                            (tar human|org)          (construed_act appropriation_act wrong_act betray_act)  (theme thief_to)  (facets reportable_crime blackmailable)
            # disinherit - testamentary act; effect ends the target's
            # heir_of belief. The dropped heir feels abandonment.
            disinherit          (motor eyes right_hand)         (tar human)              (construed_act abandonment_act wrong_act)  (abduct)
            # jilt - the chosen ending of a lover bond (the jilter breaks
            # with the jilted, typically for a class-suitable betrothal).
            # Patient cascade: abandonment_act -> grief + attachment_loss +
            # status_loss; wrong_act -> anger + humiliation + injustice -
            # the obsessive-ex pressure stack the coerce deliberation
            # affinity reads.
            jilt                (motor mouth)                   (tar human)              (construed_act abandonment_act wrong_act)  (abduct)
            # silence_witness - composite task. Implementations may
            # bubble down through kill / bribe / coerce chains depending
            # on substrate; the anchor records the composite plan that
            # was undertaken. The patient-end state (silenced) is what
            # the goal targets; the chosen leaf task is whichever the
            # actor's substrate-driven perpetration selector picks. The
            # silenced state itself is expressed as
            # {witness avoid {witness tell secret}}.
            silence_witness                                     (tar human)

            # ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
            # Leaf method-tasks - the SPECIFIC tasks an actor performs to
            # achieve an abstract parent goal (kill / coerce / expose /
            # bribe / etc.). The perpetration .hsc rows enumerate these
            # plus their substrate-rooted weights, requirements, and
            # consequences. The anchor minted at task completion is the
            # leaf-task belief itself - e.g. {actor strangle victim}, not
            # {actor kill victim /aux strangle}. The kill goal is
            # recorded separately on the consumed goal-belief; the
            # crime ledger records BOTH (goal=kill, task=strangle) so
            # detective queries can pivot on either axis.
            #
            # Where a method uses an INSTRUMENT, the act record's /aux
            # carries the instrument ENTITY (each mind's mental object for
            # it; the abs entity in the ledger) - "THAT knife", never a
            # bare kind. Showing the recovered weapon to a witness is then
            # a recognition test against their existing mental object. A
            # genuinely bare-handed method (strangle, neck_snap) has no
            # instrument and carries no aux; its evidence is the wound
            # state. For `poison` the aux is the VESSEL the dose was
            # served in (liquids are not entities); the substance is the
            # prior add_substance belief + the vessel's residue stain.
            # ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

            # Sharp-implement leaf kill-tasks. Each requires a blade /
            # pointed-blade controlled by an actor's hand.
            stab                (motor right_hand)              (tar human)  (aux object)  (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (facets reportable_crime)  (obs)
            slash               (motor right_hand)              (tar human)  (aux object)  (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (facets reportable_crime)  (obs)
            decapitate          (motor right_hand left_hand)    (tar human)  (aux object)  (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (facets reportable_crime)  (obs)

            # Blunt-implement leaf kill-tasks.
            beat_to_death       (motor right_hand left_hand legs)  (tar human)  (aux object)  (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (facets reportable_crime)  (obs)
            bludgeon            (motor right_hand left_hand)    (tar human)  (aux object)  (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (facets reportable_crime)  (obs)
            push_from_height    (motor right_hand left_hand legs)  (tar human)           (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (facets reportable_crime)  (obs)

            # Asphyxiation leaf kill-tasks. strangle is bare-handed;
            # garrotte uses cord_or_wire in hand; smother uses a soft
            # implement; hang and neck_snap are mechanical.
            strangle            (motor right_hand left_hand)    (tar human)              (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (facets reportable_crime)  (obs)
            garrotte            (motor right_hand left_hand)    (tar human)  (aux object)  (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (facets reportable_crime)  (obs)
            smother             (motor right_hand left_hand)    (tar human)  (aux object)  (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (facets reportable_crime)  (obs)
            hang                (motor right_hand left_hand legs)  (tar human)  (aux object)  (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (facets reportable_crime)  (obs)
            neck_snap           (motor right_hand left_hand)    (tar human)              (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (obs)

            # Projectile / explosive leaf kill-tasks.
            shoot               (motor right_hand eyes)         (tar human)  (aux object)  (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (obs)
            bomb                (motor right_hand)              (tar human)  (aux object)  (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (obs)

            # Chemical leaf kill-task. The /aux is the VESSEL entity the
            # dose was served in; the poison itself is a concentrated
            # `poison` fluid the killer holds, and the dose LACES the
            # victim's drink (the drink fluid's `taint` attr names the
            # poison kind). poison is the chronic / acute administering task
            # whose completion is the victim's death.
            poison                                              (tar human)  (aux object)  (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (facets reportable_crime blackmailable)

            # Hydraulic / thermal / electrical leaf kill-tasks.
            drown               (motor right_hand left_hand legs)  (tar human)           (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (obs)
            freeze              (motor right_hand)              (tar human)              (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)
            immolate            (motor right_hand)              (tar human)  (aux object)  (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (obs)
            arson               (motor right_hand)              (tar human)  (aux object)  (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)
            cook_alive          (motor right_hand)              (tar human)              (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (obs)
            electrocute         (motor right_hand)              (tar human)              (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (obs)

            # Animal-mediated leaf kill-tasks.
            unleash_animal      (motor right_hand)              (tar human)              (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)
            unleash_insect      (motor right_hand)              (tar human)              (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)

            # Trap / indirect leaf kill-tasks. death_trap is a delayed
            # mechanical trap (the actor isn't present at trigger).
            # uriah_gambit sends the victim into a fatal situation under
            # false pretense (Bible: David's order to put Uriah in the
            # front line). commission_killing delegates the act to a hired
            # killer (the murder-for-hire conspiracy - contract_killing.cc).
            death_trap          (motor right_hand)              (tar human)  (aux object)  (construed_act harm_act wrong_act betray_act)  (facets reportable_crime)
            uriah_gambit                                        (tar human)              (construed_act harm_act wrong_act betray_act)
            commission_killing                                  (tar human)  (aux human)  (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)

            # Leaf non-kill-tasks - specific methods for achieving the
            # non-kill abstract goals (steal / expose / coerce / bribe /
            # hurt / humiliate / discredit / frame / seduce). Same
            # principle: the parent task is the goal-class, the leaf
            # task is what's actually done. Where the parent task is
            # specific enough (e.g. `insult`, `discredit`) the
            # perpetration row uses the parent task directly as its
            # leaf.
            opportunist_theft   (motor legs right_hand)         (tar human)              (construed_act appropriation_act wrong_act)  (theme thief_to)  (facets reportable_crime blackmailable)
            anonymous_letter    (motor eyes right_hand legs)    (tar human)  (aux ?)     (construed_act expose_act betray_act)  (facets blackmailable)
            # report_to_police: the report_crime goal's leaf - writing and
            # delivering a crime_report letter to the police station.
            report_to_police    (motor eyes right_hand legs)    (tar ?)  (aux ?)         (construed_act honour_act)
            beating             (motor right_hand left_hand legs)  (tar human)           (construed_act harm_act wrong_act)  (theme violent_to)  (facets reportable_crime)  (obs)
            offer_bribe         (motor right_hand mouth)        (tar human)  (aux ?)     (facets blackmailable)
            plant_evidence      (motor right_hand)              (tar human)  (aux ?)     (construed_act harm_act betray_act wrong_act)  (facets reportable_crime blackmailable)
            seduction           (motor mouth legs body)         (tar human)              (construed_act intimacy_act)

            # ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
            # Speech acts - the verbal-method vocabulary. These labels are
            # NOT minted as act-record beliefs: the memory of a verbal act
            # is a SAY action belief whose @msg target carries the
            # utterance, classified by a trailing (msg_class <leaf>) arg
            # on the msg func - {actor SAY (msg ~{grievance}
            # (msg_class insult)) /aux victim}. The leaves remain real
            # task kinds because (a) deliberation goal clauses still name
            # them ({actor goal {actor confront_privately victim}} - the
            # victim stays the goal clause's target), (b) perpetration
            # rows validate their :method atoms against Tasks.mon, and
            # (c) their (construed_act ...) tags are what categorize()
            # reads off the msg_class kind when appraising the SAY
            # anchor (patient = the SAY's @msgAudience aux).
            #
            # KEEP THIS GROUP LAST in the task block: a .mon de-indent
            # resets cascaded (+) flags (the (+ task) (+ sub human) on
            # `task`), so no flat task sibling may follow this nested
            # group.
            # ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
            speech_act
                insult              (motor mouth)                   (tar human)              (construed_act slight_act)  (theme rude_to)  (abduct)
                confront_privately  (motor legs mouth)              (tar human)
                confront_publicly   (motor mouth)                   (tar human)              (construed_act expose_act)
                threaten_violence   (motor mouth)                   (tar human)  (aux ?)     (construed_act coercion_act threaten_act wrong_act)
                blackmail           (motor mouth)                   (tar human)  (aux ?)     (construed_act coercion_act wrong_act betray_act)
                public_humiliation  (motor mouth)                   (tar human)              (construed_act degrade_act wrong_act)
                spread_rumour       (motor mouth)                   (tar human)  (aux ?)     (construed_act expose_act betray_act wrong_act)